As of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98397, this can be replaced with a call to `OS::get_temp_path()` on all platforms[^1]:

```suggestion
// We need to load an occluder path because when the occluder generates,
	// it has to save to a file.
	const String occluder_path = OS::get_singleton()->get_temp_path().path_join("test_occluder.occ");
```

[^1]: `OS::get_temp_path()` is used in C++, but it's `OS.get_temp_dir()` in the scripting API.
